WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:16.177
The Venn view answers one question: who is in more than one circle?

2
00:00:16.178 --> 00:00:26.448
With all four circles selected you get the classic four-set diagram. Each number is the count of people in exactly that overlap.

3
00:00:26.448 --> 00:00:37.331
Deselect a circle and the diagram becomes area-proportional: bigger groups get bigger circles, and the overlap size is exact.

4
00:00:37.331 --> 00:00:43.159
Hover a region for details. Click it to list exactly those people.

5
00:00:43.159 --> 00:00:48.447
That takes you to People with the matching filter already applied.

6
00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:56.728
The chord diagram shows the same overlaps as flows. Each arc is a circle, and ribbon width is how many people two circles share.

7
00:00:56.728 --> 00:01:07.567
The loops that return to the same arc are people in only that circle. Hover a ribbon to see the count, click it to list the people.

8
00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:13.436
Flow is a Sankey diagram: sources on the left, circles in the middle, companies on the right.

9
00:01:13.436 --> 00:01:20.678
It shows where each circle comes from. Hover a node to trace its flows, click a company to list its people.
